{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-luk-21-1","title":"Luke 21:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ commends the poor widow. 5 He foretells the destruction of the temple, and of the city Jerusalem; 25 the signs also which shall be before the last day. 34 He exhorts them to be watchful.</p>\n<p>and saw. Mr 7:11-13; 12:41-44 the treasury. Jos 6:19,24; 1Ki 14:26; 2Ki 24:13; 2Ch 36:18; Ne 13:13; Mt 27:6 Joh 8:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-2","title":"Luke 21:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>mites. Mr 12:42; *marg:</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-3","title":"Luke 21:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Of. 4:25; 9:27; 12:44; Ac 4:27; 10:34 more. Ex 35:21-29; Mr 12:43,44; 14:8,9; 2Co 8:2,3,12; 9:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-4","title":"Luke 21:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>all. 8:43; 15:12; Ac 2:44,45; 4:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-5","title":"Luke 21:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>as. Mt 24:1,2; Mr 13:1,2; Joh 2:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-6","title":"Luke 21:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>there. 19:44-48; 1Ki 9:7-9; 2Ch 7:20-22; Isa 64:10,11; Jer 7:11-14 Jer 26:6,9,18; La 2:6-8; 4:1; 5:18; Eze 7:20-22; Da 9:26,27 Mic 3:12; Zec 11:1; 14:2; Mt 24:2; Mr 13:2; Ac 6:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-7","title":"Luke 21:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>when. 32; Da 12:6,8; Mt 24:3; Mr 13:3,4; Joh 21:21,22; Ac 1:6,7 what. 20,21,27,28; Mt 24:15,16; Mr 13:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-8","title":"Luke 21:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Take. Jer 29:8; Mt 24:4,5,11,23-25; Mr 13:5,6,21-23; 2Co 11:13-15 Eph 5:6; 2Th 2:3,9-11; 2Ti 3:13; 1Jo 4:1; 2Jo 1:7; Re 12:9 for. Joh 5:43; Ac 5:36,37; 8:9,10 and the time. or, and, The time. Mt 3:2; 4:17; Re 1:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-9","title":"Luke 21:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>when. 18,19; Ps 27:1-3; 46:1,2; 112:7; Pr 3:25,26; Isa 8:12; 51:12,13 Jer 4:19,20; Mt 24:6-8; Mr 13:7,8 but. 8,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-10","title":"Luke 21:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Nation shall.This portended the dissensions, insurrections, and mutual slaughter of the Jews, the open wars of different tetrarchies, and the civil wars in Italy between Otho and Vitellius.</p>\n<p>2Ch 15:5,6; Hag 2:21,22; Zec 14:2,3,13; Mr 13:8; Ac 2:19,20; 11:28 Heb 12:27; Re 6:2-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-11","title":"Luke 21:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>and great signs. 25-27; Mt 24:29,30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-12","title":"Luke 21:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>before. 11:49-51; Mt 10:16-25; 22:6; 23:34-36; 24:9,10; Mr 13:9-13 Joh 15:20; 16:2,3; Ac 4:3-7; 5:17-19,40; 6:12-15; 7:57-60; 8:3; 9:4 Ac 12:1-4; 16:22-26; 21:30,31; 22:30; 24:1-9; 25:1,2,11,12,22-25 Ac 26:2-11; 1Th 2:15,16; 1Pe 4:12-14; Re 2:10 for. 1Pe 2:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-13","title":"Luke 21:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Php 1:28; 1Th 3:3,4; 2Th 1:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-14","title":"Luke 21:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>12:11,12; Mt 10:19,20; Mr 13:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-15","title":"Luke 21:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>I will. 24:45; Ex 4:11,12; Pr 2:6; Jer 1:9; Ac 2:4; 4:8-13,31-33; Eph 6:19 Col 4:3,4; Jas 1:5 which. Ac 6:10; 24:25; 26:28; 2Ti 4:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-16","title":"Luke 21:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>ye shall. Jer 9:4; 12:6; Mic 7:5,6; Mt 10:21; Mr 13:12 and some. Ac 7:59; 12:2; 26:10,11; Re 2:13; 6:9; 12:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-17","title":"Luke 21:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>ye. Mt 10:22; 24:9; Mr 13:13; Joh 7:7; 15:19; 17:14 for. 6:22; Mt 5:11; Joh 15:21; Ac 9:16; 2Co 4:5,11; 12:10; Php 1:29 1Pe 4:14; Re 2:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-18","title":"Luke 21:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>12:7; 1Sa 14:45; 25:29; 2Sa 14:11; Mt 10:30; Ac 27:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-19","title":"Luke 21:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>8:15; Ps 27:13,14; 37:7; 40:1; Ro 2:7; 5:3; 8:25; 15:4; 1Th 1:3 2Th 3:5; Heb 6:11,15; 10:36; Jas 1:3; 5:7-11; Re 1:9; 2:2,3; 3:10 Re 13:10; 14:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-20","title":"Luke 21:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>7; 19:43; Da 9:27; Mt 24:15; Mr 13:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-21","title":"Luke 21:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>flee.Accordingly, when Cestius Gallus came against Jerusalem, and unexpectedly raised the siege, Josephus states, that many of the noble Jews departed out of the city, as out of a sinking ship; and when Vespasian afterwards drew towards it, a great multitude fled to the mountains. And we learn from Eusebius, and Epiphanius, that at this juncture, all who believed in Christ left Jerusalem, and removed to Pella, and other places beyond Jordan; and so escaped the general shipwreck of their country, that we do not read of one who perished in Jerusalem.</p>\n<p>17:31-33; Ge 19:17,26; Ex 9:20,21; Pr 22:3; Mt 24:16; Mr 13:15 and let them. Nu 16:26; Jer 6:1; 35:11; 37:12; Re 18:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-22","title":"Luke 21:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>the days. Isa 34:8; 61:2; Jer 51:6; Ro 2:5; 2Pe 2:9; 3:7 all. Le 26:14-33; De 28:15-68; 29:19-28; 32:34,43; Ps 69:22-28; 149:7-9 Isa 65:12-16; Da 9:26,27; Zec 11:1-3; 14:1,2; Mal 4:1; Mr 13:19,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-23","title":"Luke 21:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>woe. 23:29; De 28:56,57; La 4:10; Heb 9:12-17; 13:16; Mt 24:19; Mr 13:17 great. 19:27,43; Mt 21:41,44; 1Th 2:16; Heb 10:26-31; Jas 5:1; 1Pe 4:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-24","title":"Luke 21:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>led. De 28:64-68 Jerusalem. Isa 5:5; 63:18; La 1:15; Re 11:2 until. Isa 66:12,19; Da 9:27; 12:7; Mal 1:11; Ro 11:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-25","title":"Luke 21:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>signs. Isa 13:10,13,14; 24:23; Jer 4:23; Eze 32:7,8; Joe 2:30,31 Am 8:9,10; Mt 24:29; 27:45; Mr 13:24,26; 15:33; Ac 2:19; 2Pe 3:10-12 Re 6:12-14; 20:11 upon. Da 12:1 with. Isa 22:4,5; Mic 7:4 the sea. Ps 46:3; 93:3,4; Isa 5:30; 51:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-26","title":"Luke 21:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>hearts. Le 26:36; De 28:32-34,65-67; Heb 10:26,27 for the. Mt 24:29; Mr 13:25; 2Pe 3:10-12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-27","title":"Luke 21:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>see. Da 7:13; Mt 24:30; 26:64; Mr 13:26; Ac 1:9-11; Re 1:7; 14:14 with. Mt 16:27,28; 25:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-28","title":"Luke 21:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>look. Ps 98:5-9; Isa 12:1-3; 25:8,9; 60:1,2 redemption. Ro 8:19,23; Eph 1:14; 4:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-29","title":"Luke 21:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>Behold. Mt 24:32-35; Mr 13:28-30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-31","title":"Luke 21:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>when. 12:51-57; Mt 16:1-4 the kingdom. Heb 10:37; Jas 5:9; 1Pe 4:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-32","title":"Luke 21:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>11:50,51; Mt 16:28; 23:36; 24:34; Mr 13:30</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-33","title":"Luke 21:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>Ps 102:26; Isa 40:8; 51:6; Mt 5:18; 24:35; Mr 13:31; 1Pe 1:25 2Pe 3:7-14; Re 20:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-34","title":"Luke 21:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>take. 8; 17:3; Mr 13:9; Heb 12:15 your hearts. 12:45; Le 10:9; Pr 21:4; Isa 28:7; 56:10-12; Ho 4:11; Ro 13:11-13 1Th 5:6-8; 1Pe 4:3-7 surfeiting. De 29:19; 1Sa 25:36; Isa 28:1-3; 1Co 5:11; 6:10; Ga 5:20 cares. 8:14; 10:41; Mt 13:22; Mr 4:19; Php 4:6 that day. 12:46; Ps 35:8; Mt 24:39-50; Mr 13:35-37; 1Th 5:2-4; 2Pe 3:10,14 Re 3:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-35","title":"Luke 21:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>as. Ps 11:6; Ec 9:12; Isa 24:17,18; Jer 48:43,44; Re 16:15 dwell. 17:37; Ge 7:4; Ac 17:26 of the whole earth.Or, \"of this whole land; the land of Judea, on which these heavy judgments were to fall.\"</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-36","title":"Luke 21:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>Watch. 12:37-40; Mt 24:42; 25:13; 26:41; Mr 13:33,37; 1Co 16:13; 2Ti 4:5 1Pe 4:7; 5:8 pray. 18:1; Job 27:10; Ac 10:2; Eph 6:18,19; Col 4:2; 1Th 5:17 accounted. 20:35; 2Th 1:5,6 stand. Ps 1:5; Mal 3:2; Eph 6:13,14; 1Jo 2:28; Jude 1:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-37","title":"Luke 21:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>the day time. 22:39; Mt 21:17; Mr 11:12; Joh 12:1 mount. 19:37; Zec 14:4; Mt 26:30; Ac 1:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-luk-21-38","title":"Luke 21:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"LUK","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<